From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:56:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: ASoC: qcom: sdw: deprepare the SoundWire stream across
 system suspend

qcom_snd_sdw_trigger() disables the stream on SUSPEND and on RESUME
calls sdw_prepare_stream() on the DISABLED stream, which re-programs the
ports but, by design, skips the bus parameter computation. That is
enough for the WSA884x speakers on their own buses, but not for the
WCD9378 headphone stream on the Glymur multi-master bus (swr2 with swr1's
lanes, per-port BPS computed in qcom_swrm_compute_params()): after one
s2idle cycle with the headphone PCM held open, the codec's PDE 47 no
longer reaches PS0, neither on resume nor on any later stream start:

  snd_soc_sdca_class_function snd_soc_sdca.SimpleJack.0: PDE 47: pde transition 3 -> 0 failed: -110

and the codec reports a Function_Fault each time. The headphones stay
silent until reboot; a function reset does not recover them.

Deprepare the stream after disabling it, and prepare it on RESUME as a
new stream, with the bus parameters computed again. hw_free leaves a
deprepared stream alone.

On the ASUS Zenbook A16, with this and the stream restarted before DAPM
resumes the codec, the headphones play after every resume: 7 of 7
held-stream s2idle cycles, 28 of 28 tone bursts after them verified on a
line-in capture; without it, 0 of 6 cycles.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

 sound/soc/qcom/sdw.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sdw.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sdw.c
index 578d29777626..e7c325f92b54 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sdw.c
@@ -128,7 +128,8 @@ static int qcom_snd_sdw_restart(struct sdw_stream_runtime *sruntime)
 {
 	int ret;
 
-	if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_DISABLED) {
+	if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_DEPREPARED ||
+	    sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_DISABLED) {
 		/* Re-applies the port setup; the bus may have been reset. */
 		ret = sdw_prepare_stream(sruntime);
 		if (ret)
@@ -153,10 +154,13 @@ static int qcom_snd_sdw_restart(struct sdw_stream_runtime *sruntime)
  * otherwise stays enabled while the PCM is suspended: the controller enters
  * and leaves clock stop with its data ports enabled, and the ports carry
  * whatever the macro sends the moment the bus clock restarts, before the
- * bus has been checked. Disable the stream on SUSPEND and program and enable
- * it again on RESUME. The trigger order (link first on RESUME, last on
- * SUSPEND, codec unmute after the DAI triggers) keeps the ports enabled
- * whenever an amplifier is unmuted.
+ * bus has been checked. Disable and deprepare the stream on SUSPEND, and
+ * prepare and enable it again on RESUME, as a new stream would be: a
+ * stream only disabled and re-prepared (sdw_prepare_stream() on a DISABLED
+ * stream skips the bus parameter computation) does not come back on every
+ * bus. The trigger order (link first on RESUME, last on SUSPEND, codec
+ * unmute after the DAI triggers) keeps the ports enabled whenever an
+ * amplifier is unmuted.
  *
  * Return: 0 or errno
  */
@@ -175,10 +179,18 @@ int qcom_snd_sdw_trigger(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, int cmd,
 		return 0;
 
 	switch (cmd) {
-	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_SUSPEND:
-		if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_ENABLED)
-			return sdw_disable_stream(sruntime);
+	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_SUSPEND: {
+		int ret;
+
+		if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_ENABLED) {
+			ret = sdw_disable_stream(sruntime);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+		if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_DISABLED)
+			return sdw_deprepare_stream(sruntime);
 		break;
+	}
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_RESUME:
 		return qcom_snd_sdw_restart(sruntime);
 	default:
@@ -206,7 +218,7 @@ int qcom_snd_sdw_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
-	 * Already prepared, but left DISABLED by a system suspend whose
+	 * Already prepared, but left deprepared by a system suspend whose
 	 * RESUME trigger failed or never came (user space prepares
 	 * instead): program and enable the ports again.
 	 */
@@ -275,10 +287,11 @@ int qcom_snd_sdw_hw_free(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream, bool *stream_prepa
 
 	sruntime = qcom_snd_sdw_get_stream(substream);
 	if (sruntime && *stream_prepared) {
-		/* A stream disabled for system suspend is only deprepared. */
+		/* A stream deprepared for system suspend needs nothing more. */
 		if (sruntime->state == SDW_STREAM_ENABLED)
 			sdw_disable_stream(sruntime);
-		sdw_deprepare_stream(sruntime);
+		if (sruntime->state != SDW_STREAM_DEPREPARED)
+			sdw_deprepare_stream(sruntime);
 		*stream_prepared = false;
 	}
 
